prompts.walk:
Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: ONE 12-frame in-place walking animation atlas for the EXACT reference chicken.
References: image 1 is the approved high resolution identity; image 2 is the normalized neutral canvas and contact alignment; image 3/4 are existing states for color/line/body consistency only. Preserve this specific round cream hen, salmon comb, brown rounded outline, golden three-toed feet, dot eye, 3 tail feathers and one simple scalloped near wing. Same cream/yellow shading, no extra feather detail. Do not redesign the character.
Make exactly FOUR columns by THREE rows, twelve equal cells, reading order. Prefer 1440x840 sheet, each cell 360x280, on real transparent alpha, fully alpha-zero outside silhouettes with no stray colored specks. No borders or frame numbers. The chicken faces LEFT in the same slightly elevated oblique side view as the reference. Every cell has identical camera, body size and placement. Body (excluding tail) remains approximately 180 px wide, pelvis centered in the same place. Neutral near toe contact = (180,230), far toe contact approximately (131,219), preserving the depth offset. Tail and head must retain proportions and remain stable.
Primary action: natural biped CHICKEN WALK IN PLACE, not moving the whole sprite through the cells. Clearly articulate TWO separate yellow feet with tiny visible ankle bends, alternating weight support. One foot stays on the ground and pushes backward while the other lifts, toes curl, swings forward and lands. No sliding, no duplicated poses. Do not hide all the legs under the body, do not animate by rotating/shaking the whole chicken. Tiny 1-3px torso rise/fall allowed, no body stretching.
Twelve unique cycle phases, phase interval 30 degrees; total 1 second at 12fps:
00 near foot forward touching down, far foot behind preparing to lift;
01 near foot planted beginning backward push, far foot toe-off with ankle bent;
02 near foot planted, far foot lifted and swinging forward;
03 near foot under torso bearing weight, far foot raised passing the planted foot;
04 near foot moving toward rear stance, far foot reaching forward with toes opening;
05 near foot near toe-off, far foot just above forward landing;
06 far foot lands forward, near foot behind preparing to lift;
07 far foot planted beginning backward push, near foot toe-off with ankle bent;
08 far foot planted, near foot lifted and swinging forward;
09 far foot under torso bearing weight, near foot raised passing planted foot;
10 far foot moving toward rear stance, near foot reaching forward;
11 far foot near toe-off, near foot just above forward landing approaching phase00.
Projected travel direction is diagonally left and slightly toward viewer, about vector(-24,+12) pixels PER CYCLE at the 360x280 reference scale. Each foot's fore-aft excursion approximately 12px on either side of its neutral site, swing lift about 7px. The image root/pelvis remains stationary; actual scene translation is done later by code. Last frame is NOT a copy of first.
Keep eye and wing nearly fixed, avoid blinking or flapping. No scene, ground, shadow, fences, products, food, eggs, feed, clocks, arrows, trails, text, checkerboard, backdrop or extraneous pixels. Feet are part of the animal; ALL shadows omitted for separate delivery. Maintain enough transparent padding so no sprite touches another cell. All twelve silhouettes must be individually complete.
